{
  "source_commit": "a986de180b145237716373857a01972ba384a3b5",
  "harness_commit": "WS4 step 0 (this commit)",
  "measurement_scope": "Lite write-amplification counting harness (zig build lite-write-amplification, Debug), re-run on perf/lwa-ws4-indexed-commit after adding stage-attribution scopes at the real indexed-write call sites that the original baseline left bucketed under 'other': lite/index_storage.zig's virtual-filesystem-on-native-catalog adapter (writeFileReserved -> vfs_write, appendFileAbsolute -> vfs_append, renameAbsolute -> vfs_rename, deleteFileAbsolute -> vfs_delete, syncContentsAbsolute/syncParentAbsolute -> vfs_sync, NativeAtomicWriteSink.finish/finishSource/finishMapped -> vfs_finish), lite/artifact_source.zig Registry.open's non-pooled lease-pointer commit (-> artifact_lease), persistent.zig PersistentIndex.MainTxn.commit (-> main_txn_commit), and the one production LSM-backend WAL-append call site in lsm_backend.zig's WriteCoordinator-like append() helper (-> lsm_backend_wal; the other 6 wal_mod.appendStateWithOptions call sites in that file are test fixtures, not production call sites, and were left unscoped). Same workload as the baseline receipt: 128 single-doc updates, 1 KiB changing text per update, primary_only deletes the default full_text_index_v0 index, indexed/indexed_8_writers keep it and use sync_level=full_index.",
  "known_limitations": [
    "artifact_pin, lsm_wal, progress, status_snapshot, replay_retirement, and (newly) main_txn_commit and lsm_backend_wal all still read zero for this workload, for the same underlying reason the baseline receipt noted: the default full_text_index_v0 index's segments stay small enough that PersistentIndex.indexSegmentOwned's segment-file/segment-WAL branch and lsm_backend.zig's production WAL-append call site are never taken at this size. This is now a *complete* attribution for the calling thread, not a gap: see calling-thread 'other' below, which is 0 for both primary_only and indexed in this receipt.",
    "Numbers differ from the original write-amplification-baseline.json (3.0 primary-only / 66.84 indexed calling-thread syncs/update) because this worktree's base (perf/lwa-integration, a986de180b) already includes WS1's native-commit-protocol work (3->2 syncs/commit) and WS5's retirement-off-the-ack-path work, both landed after the original baseline was measured. This receipt is the correct 'before' point for WS4's own work, measured on the same commit WS4 started from, not a regression or an improvement attributable to attribution tracing itself (adding wal_trace.scope() calls is dead code outside test binaries and changes no production control flow).",
    "maintenance_lease_acquired and serving_runtime_refresh still read zero: the harness opens Lite directly through the capi.openLiteHandleWithRuntime embedding seam with a .manual BackendRuntime, bypassing capi/lite_connection.zig's Owner/connection-pool layer.",
    "indexed_8_writers' per-stage totals remain numerically identical to the single-writer indexed case for the same reason as the baseline: both measure the same total update count (128); the harness counts operations, not latency."
  ],
  "receipt_comparison": "Calling-thread 'other' drops from 3873 (30.26/update) in the original baseline to 0 in this receipt for the indexed mode: every calling-thread sync is now attributed to a named stage. The single largest indexed calling-thread contributor is artifact_lease (2034 syncs, 46% of the 4424 calling-thread syncs/128 updates = 34.5625/update total), i.e. the artifact lease Registry.open creates for every small full-text segment publish -- this is exactly the cost WS4 step 2 (no artifact lease for small segments) targets. The four lite/index_storage.zig virtual-filesystem stages (vfs_write 256, vfs_append 542, vfs_delete 282, vfs_finish 542; vfs_rename and vfs_sync both read 0 for this workload) account for the rest: 1622 syncs, ~37% of the total. primary_commit (768 syncs, ~17%) is the primary document write's own commit, unaffected by WS4. main_txn_commit and lsm_backend_wal read 0: MainTxn.commit's own call does not itself touch the leaf sync counters (it delegates to the LSM backend's write-transaction commit, whose actual durable I/O is already captured by the vfs_* stages above, since Lite's LSM backend stores its files through lite/index_storage.zig), and the LSM backend's one production WAL-append call site is not reached at this index size.",
